  "Churned_Credit": "1. Has-funds: none. This is a platform ledger line, not a product has-funds client. There is no has-funds true/false or API-failure branch. 2. Product: none. Billing writes the credit, debit, Stripe, churn, or tax line itself. 3. Bill: no producer POST /bill, so there is no fundCheck branch and no 422 from a product bill. 4. After: the ledger row is the outcome. A failed platform write means the line is not recorded.",
  "Stripe_Refund": "1. Has-funds: none. This is a platform ledger line, not a product has-funds client. There is no has-funds true/false or API-failure branch. 2. Product: none. Billing writes the credit, debit, Stripe, churn, or tax line itself. 3. Bill: no producer POST /bill, so there is no fundCheck branch and no 422 from a product bill. 4. After: the ledger row is the outcome. A failed platform write means the line is not recorded.",
  "outbound_group_sms": "1. Has-funds: before the group SMS, lc-phone calls location or agency has-funds. If rebilling is off, the has-funds call is skipped and treated as has funds. If has-funds returns hasFunds false, the product is blocked. If the has-funds API throws, the catch returns hasFunds true and the product continues. A false result blocks the send. 2. Product: Twilio sends the group message. If send fails, /bill is not called. 3. Bill: after the message, billGroupSms calls BillingService.billOtherMessages. If /bill succeeds, the wallet debit is written. If /bill fails, the charge is not written. The product already ran, so that failure does not undo it. fundCheck is false, so /bill does not check funds again. 4. After bill: success debits the group message. Failure leaves the sent message in place with no debit.",
